      "text": "Faith is a principle of action and of power, and by it one can command the elements, heal the sick, and influence any number of circumstances when occasion warrants (Jacob 4:4–7). Even more important, by faith one obtains a remission of sins and eventually can stand in the presence of God.",
      "references": [
        {
          "text": "Jacob 4:4–7",
          "start": 166,
          "end": 177,
          "parsed": {
            "volume": "bofm",
            "bookKey": "jacob",
            "book": "jacob",
            "chapter": 4,
